<p><strong>To advertise on ChatGPT, create and verify an account in OpenAI Ads Manager Beta, choose a campaign objective and budget, organise ad groups around clear intent themes, add approved creative and a relevant landing page, then submit the campaign for review.</strong></p>
<p>Before setup, read the <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-india">complete ChatGPT Ads India guide</a>. It explains current availability, placements, privacy and the role of this beta channel.</p>

<h2>1. Confirm availability and define the business result</h2>
<p>OpenAI currently lists India as available for self-service access. Start at <a href="https://ads.openai.com/">Ads Manager</a>, but do not create a campaign until the result is clear. Choose a primary outcome such as qualified website traffic, a lead submission, a booking or reach among a relevant audience.</p>
<p>Write down how the sales team will judge a qualified enquiry. This prevents the campaign from being optimized around clicks that do not help the business.</p>

<h2>2. Set up and verify the advertiser account</h2>
<p>OpenAI's <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001224-quickstart-launch-your-first-campaign">official campaign quickstart</a> describes the account steps: sign in with a work email, add the brand identity, configure billing, complete account verification and invite only the team members who need access.</p>
<p>Use a company-controlled email address and document who owns billing, creative approval and reporting. Do not leave a production advertising account tied only to a temporary contractor login.</p>

<h2>3. Choose the campaign objective and budget type</h2>
<p>Ads Manager currently offers CPM, CPC and oCPC objectives. Use CPM when reach is the main goal, CPC when qualified site traffic is the main goal, and oCPC when conversion tracking is ready and the campaign should optimize toward a supported downstream action.</p>
<p>You can use a campaign-total budget or a daily budget. A daily budget is an average over a seven-day period, not an absolute same-day ceiling. OpenAI says individual-day spend can be higher or lower while remaining within the applicable seven-day rules. Read the <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-cost-india">India cost and budgeting guide</a> before setting the amount.</p>

<h2>4. Select dates, countries and platforms</h2>
<p>Set dates that give the campaign enough time to collect meaningful signals. Choose only the countries you can genuinely serve. Ads Manager can also target supported platforms such as iOS, Android and web.</p>
<p>Do not expand geography simply to increase impressions. A larger audience is not useful when the landing page, fulfilment team or sales process cannot support it.</p>

<h2>5. Build intent-led ad groups</h2>
<p>An ad group should contain ads connected to one clear theme. For a digital agency, useful themes might include website visibility, local discovery and paid-media efficiency. Each theme should have its own relevant creative and landing-page message.</p>
<p>Advertisers can provide context hints that describe conversations, topics or keywords where the offer may be relevant. OpenAI says these hints guide matching but are not exact-match keywords and do not guarantee delivery.</p>

<h2>6. Set the bid strategy carefully</h2>
<p>Depending on the campaign, Ads Manager may offer automated or manual bid controls. A maximum bid is a ceiling, not a predicted result. Avoid treating a suggested starting bid as a fixed market price or a guaranteed average cost.</p>
<p>During an early test, balance delivery with a clear commercial limit. The right bid depends on what a qualified visit, lead or customer is worth to the business.</p>

<h2>7. Create specific ad variations</h2>
<p>Each ad can include a title, description, image and landing page. Make the offer precise, useful and supportable. Instead of “Grow Your Business,” test a message that identifies the service, customer and next step.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Use one benefit or customer problem per variation.</li>
    <li>Match the image and copy to the landing page.</li>
    <li>Avoid unsupported superlatives, urgency or implied endorsements.</li>
    <li>Check the advertiser identity, spelling and mobile crop.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Prepare the landing page and measurement</h2>
<p>The landing page should complete the promise made by the ad. Repeat the specific offer, explain who it is for, show relevant proof, answer common objections and use one primary conversion action.</p>
<p>Configure conversion measurement where appropriate and add static UTM parameters so analytics can identify ChatGPT Ads traffic. Test forms, phone links, thank-you states and lead notifications before launch.</p>

<h2>9. Submit for review and confirm delivery</h2>
<p>Submit the campaign and ads for review. After approval, check whether each item is serving. If it is not, review account verification, billing, dates, budget, campaign status and the reason shown in Ads Manager before making changes.</p>

<h2>10. Review business signals, not only clicks</h2>
<p>Ads Manager can report impressions, clicks, spend, CTR, average CPC, average CPM and conversions. Combine those numbers with landing-page conversion rate, qualified leads, sales outcomes and customer acquisition cost.</p>
<p>Change one major variable at a time. Keep a record of creative, targeting, bid and landing-page updates so the team can learn what affected performance.</p>

<h2>Pre-launch checklist</h2>
<ol>
    <li>One campaign objective and one primary conversion.</li>
    <li>Verified account, working billing and correct team access.</li>
    <li>Focused geography, dates, platforms and budget.</li>
    <li>Themed ad groups with relevant context hints.</li>
    <li>Several distinct, policy-compliant ads.</li>
    <li>A fast landing page with tested tracking and lead delivery.</li>
</ol>

